Okay.

1387
01:03:20,600 --> 01:03:21,333
Now it's fun.

1388
01:03:21,333 --> 01:03:21,800
It's fun.

1389
01:03:31,300 --> 01:03:32,233
Nervous?

1390
01:03:33,066 --> 01:03:34,166
Not really.

1391
01:03:35,400 --> 01:03:36,400
I won't make things awkward with you.

1392
01:03:39,466 --> 01:03:40,700
Then I'll go first.

1393
01:03:45,866 --> 01:03:48,566
Actually, I didn't bring the Moonstone.

1394
01:03:49,866 --> 01:03:50,600
Because I hoped

1395
01:03:50,633 --> 01:03:51,366
we could have

1396
01:03:51,400 --> 01:03:52,866
a more relaxed vibe,

1397
01:03:52,866 --> 01:03:55,133
just like when we chatted the other day.

1398
01:03:55,800 --> 01:03:58,200
I'm here just to tell you

1399
01:03:58,200 --> 01:04:00,100
that those declarations I made
when I came back this time

1400
01:04:00,100 --> 01:04:03,300
were the first time I've ever done
something like that in my life.

1401
01:04:04,466 --> 01:04:05,566
What I thought at the time was,

1402
01:04:05,600 --> 01:04:06,833
no matter the outcome,

1403
01:04:06,833 --> 01:04:08,900
if you could truly cast one vote for me,

1404
01:04:08,900 --> 01:04:10,900
I would have been really happy already.

1405
01:04:12,466 --> 01:04:14,566
Today is the last day on the island,

1406
01:04:14,600 --> 01:04:16,800
but I feel like starting today,

1407
01:04:16,800 --> 01:04:18,233
it's a brand new day.

1408
01:04:21,333 --> 01:04:22,800
If fate allows,

1409
01:04:22,833 --> 01:04:24,533
we can keep in touch

1410
01:04:24,533 --> 01:04:25,600
and keep getting to know each other.

1411
01:04:28,033 --> 01:04:29,333
And finally,

1412
01:04:29,333 --> 01:04:31,800
I prepared a little keepsake.

1413
01:04:32,600 --> 01:04:35,133
It's a small seashell.

1414
01:04:37,800 --> 01:04:41,100
Before I came, I told myself

1415
01:04:41,100 --> 01:04:42,766
that no matter what,

1416
01:04:42,800 --> 01:04:44,733
I really wanted to find
the most beautiful shell

1417
01:04:44,733 --> 01:04:46,433
I could find by the sea myself

1418
01:04:46,466 --> 01:04:48,733
and give it to someone I really like.

1419
01:04:48,733 --> 01:04:50,933
Give it to someone I really like.

1420
01:04:52,833 --> 01:04:53,366
This seashell,

1421
01:04:53,400 --> 01:04:55,266
I wrote your name, 'Xia', on the back.

1422
01:04:58,533 --> 01:05:00,933
I used a blue pen.

1423
01:05:01,000 --> 01:05:03,666
[Blue XIA]

1424
01:05:05,833 --> 01:05:06,533
When I first arrived,

1425
01:05:06,533 --> 01:05:06,866
on the first day,

1426
01:05:06,900 --> 01:05:08,366
you wore a white dress.

1427
01:05:08,400 --> 01:05:09,133
Everyone knew

1428
01:05:09,133 --> 01:05:10,833
you wore a white dress.

1429
01:05:10,866 --> 01:05:12,566
But I remember on the second day,

1430
01:05:12,600 --> 01:05:14,066
you wore a blue dress.

1431
01:05:14,700 --> 01:05:15,233
Yes.

1432
01:05:15,266 --> 01:05:16,333
And it just so happened
that on the second day,

1433
01:05:16,333 --> 01:05:18,233
I was also wearing blue.

1434
01:05:18,266 --> 01:05:20,000
That's why I used blue ink

1435
01:05:20,033 --> 01:05:21,233
to write your name.

1436
01:05:22,733 --> 01:05:24,266
I just thought it'd be
a nice little keepsake.

1437
01:05:24,300 --> 01:05:25,733
Please take it.

1438
01:05:27,600 --> 01:05:28,833
Thank you.

1439
01:05:29,233 --> 01:05:30,833
[A little keepsake
holds tons of memories.]

1440
01:05:35,900 --> 01:05:37,833
This seashell is really nice.

1441
01:05:37,866 --> 01:05:40,200
Did you find it here by the sea?

1442
01:05:40,233 --> 01:05:42,500
Yeah.

1443
01:05:43,866 --> 01:05:45,566
I've never even seen seashells
on this beach.

1444
01:05:45,600 --> 01:05:47,133
Yeah, it was pretty hard to find it.

1445
01:05:47,133 --> 01:05:49,000
I've been looking for it
these past few days.

1446
01:05:50,333 --> 01:05:51,266
Okay.

1447
01:05:51,300 --> 01:05:52,900
Okay, I've said what I wanted to say.

1448
01:05:55,400 --> 01:05:57,100
Now it's my turn, right?

1449
01:05:57,100 --> 01:05:57,833
Okay.

1450
01:05:59,133 --> 01:06:00,133
Alright, Xia (Xia Boyan).

1451
01:06:00,133 --> 01:06:01,566
I was thinking

1452
01:06:03,266 --> 01:06:05,966
about how to talk to you.

1453
01:06:06,533 --> 01:06:07,533
But in the end, I still felt

1454
01:06:07,533 --> 01:06:08,933
it's best if I just be myself.

1455
01:06:08,933 --> 01:06:11,200
I shouldn't change myself

1456
01:06:11,233 --> 01:06:13,700
for anyone I like.

1457
01:06:17,933 --> 01:06:19,200
Xiaxia (Xia Boyan),

1458
01:06:19,233 --> 01:06:22,033
today, I didn't prepare
too many sweet words.

1459
01:06:22,033 --> 01:06:23,666
I'll try my best
not to make you feel awkward.

1460
01:06:23,666 --> 01:06:25,200
I'll consider your feelings, too.

1461
01:06:25,233 --> 01:06:26,900
What I want more

1462
01:06:26,900 --> 01:06:29,200
is to take this chance
to sincerely thank you

1463
01:06:29,233 --> 01:06:30,233
because I never expected

1464
01:06:30,233 --> 01:06:32,300
that in this show,

1465
01:06:32,300 --> 01:06:33,433
I'd actually meet someone

1466
01:06:33,466 --> 01:06:35,466
I truly fell for.

1467
01:06:37,066 --> 01:06:38,766
We competed together so many times,

1468
01:06:38,800 --> 01:06:40,200
won the championship together,

1469
01:06:41,033 --> 01:06:42,233
went into the city to have fun,

1470
01:06:42,233 --> 01:06:43,733
skied together,

1471
01:06:43,733 --> 01:06:45,033
and filmed little videos together.

1472
01:06:45,066 --> 01:06:46,800
I feel good.

1473
01:06:46,833 --> 01:06:47,466
Good.

1474
01:06:47,466 --> 01:06:50,966
We ate grilled sausages and your favorite
scallion-free roast duck.

1475
01:06:52,800 --> 01:06:53,666
No scallion taste.

1476
01:06:54,900 --> 01:06:56,433
And I listened to you talk a bunch

1477
01:06:56,466 --> 01:06:58,300
of internet slang
I couldn't understand at all.

1478
01:07:03,233 --> 01:07:04,933
All of these things really moved me.

1479
01:07:04,933 --> 01:07:07,833
Right now, this is how I feel about you:

1480
01:07:07,866 --> 01:07:11,400
You're still a mystery,
a big question mark.

1481
01:07:15,900 --> 01:07:17,733
Just when I think

1482
01:07:17,733 --> 01:07:19,266
I've gotten to know you pretty well,

1483
01:07:19,300 --> 01:07:20,233
I also realize

1484
01:07:20,266 --> 01:07:24,400
there's still so much I don't know.

1485
01:07:24,433 --> 01:07:27,133
The flower I'm giving you today
is called 'Endless Summer'.

1486
01:07:27,133 --> 01:07:30,366
Its meaning is just like your name,

1487
01:07:30,400 --> 01:07:31,600
and just like this summer-

1488
01:07:31,600 --> 01:07:34,700
even if we're apart for a while,

1489
01:07:34,700 --> 01:07:37,200
I believe we'll meet again.

1490
01:07:37,233 --> 01:07:38,366
No matter what,

1491
01:07:41,833 --> 01:07:45,266
my only wish right now is

1492
01:07:45,266 --> 01:07:49,300
to take more time to get to know you

1493
01:07:49,300 --> 01:07:50,766
in a relaxed, genuine, and happy way

1494
01:07:50,800 --> 01:07:52,800
so you can see the real me, too.

1495
01:07:52,800 --> 01:07:53,933
Whatever happens,

1496
01:07:53,933 --> 01:07:55,666
I really hope I get this chance.

1497
01:07:58,533 --> 01:08:00,633
I'll truly cherish it.

1498
01:08:03,233 --> 01:08:04,233
Thank you.

1499
01:08:04,233 --> 01:08:05,833
Did you write this yourself?

1500
01:08:06,266 --> 01:08:06,766
Yeah.

1501
01:08:14,266 --> 01:08:16,266
This is how I really feel.

1502
01:08:19,700 --> 01:08:21,333
I didn't bring the Moonstone with me.

1503
01:08:27,933 --> 01:08:29,633
First, let me talk to Jerry (Wang Yubo).

1504
01:08:31,033 --> 01:08:33,233
I think you're really sweet.

1505
01:08:33,233 --> 01:08:35,166
You're especially pure-hearted,

1506
01:08:35,200 --> 01:08:38,066
without any bad intentions.

1507
01:08:38,066 --> 01:08:38,966
At the same time,

1508
01:08:40,300 --> 01:08:42,000
you show great respect for everyone,

1509
01:08:42,033 --> 01:08:44,066
and you get along well with everybody.

1510
01:08:45,666 --> 01:08:47,766
During these past two days,

1511
01:08:47,800 --> 01:08:49,433
I felt you're actually

1512
01:08:52,200 --> 01:08:53,800
quite a sensitive person.

1513
01:08:54,733 --> 01:08:57,433
You have a lot on your mind
that you want to say.

1514
01:08:57,466 --> 01:09:01,333
I hope you can be a bit happier

1515
01:09:01,333 --> 01:09:02,566
during this journey

1516
01:09:02,600 --> 01:09:06,000
and that you can be happy every day
after leaving the island, too.

1517
01:09:08,866 --> 01:09:09,600
Just like what you wrote for me,

1518
01:09:09,633 --> 01:09:10,666
that 'smile'.

1519
01:09:10,666 --> 01:09:12,366
Yes, you must smile.

1520
01:09:12,400 --> 01:09:14,733
Just like how you were

1521
01:09:14,733 --> 01:09:16,666
in the first couple of days
when we had just met.

1522
01:09:16,700 --> 01:09:18,966
Be more confident and smile.

1523
01:09:19,733 --> 01:09:21,033
Okay.

1524
01:09:23,233 --> 01:09:25,100
Now, to Vinson (Wei Zisheng).

1525
01:09:26,833 --> 01:09:28,666
To be honest, in these couple of days,

1526
01:09:28,666 --> 01:09:31,500
I didn't really understand you.

1527
01:09:32,266 --> 01:09:34,300
You were also a big question mark for me.

1528
01:09:34,400 --> 01:09:35,000
[Same Question Mark]

1529
01:09:35,000 --> 01:09:37,500
Every day kept changing.

1530
01:09:37,500 --> 01:09:40,200
Maybe on our first day out of the island,

1531
01:09:40,233 --> 01:09:42,266
when we went out to have fun,

1532
01:09:42,266 --> 01:09:43,600
I suddenly realized

1533
01:09:43,633 --> 01:09:44,933
Vinson (Wei Zisheng) doesn't seem

1534
01:09:44,933 --> 01:09:45,966
to be hard to understand.

1535
01:09:46,333 --> 01:09:48,666
You actually seem quite lively and cute.

1536
01:09:48,700 --> 01:09:50,733
But then on the second day, I felt again

1537
01:09:52,733 --> 01:09:55,433
that maybe you aren't exactly
how I imagined.

1538
01:09:55,466 --> 01:09:56,566
So it feels like

1539
01:09:56,600 --> 01:09:58,133
you've actually been
a question mark all along.

1540
01:09:58,500 --> 01:09:59,700
But I can tell

1541
01:09:59,700 --> 01:10:01,800
you're a very thoughtful,

1542
01:10:01,833 --> 01:10:03,700
very opinionated person.

1543
01:10:03,700 --> 01:10:06,966
You said you wanted
to meet someone on this island

1544
01:10:07,000 --> 01:10:08,600
who would like you,

1545
01:10:09,233 --> 01:10:11,233
but instead, you chose

1546
01:10:11,233 --> 01:10:12,300
someone you like.

1547
01:10:12,300 --> 01:10:13,433
I think this is exactly

1548
01:10:13,466 --> 01:10:15,300
what you just said about being yourself.

1549
01:10:17,833 --> 01:10:17,966
Right?

1550
01:10:18,000 --> 01:10:18,800
Yeah.

1551
01:10:18,800 --> 01:10:19,866
So,

1552
01:10:19,866 --> 01:10:22,966
I hope that while you stay true
to yourself in the future,

1553
01:10:23,000 --> 01:10:26,700
you can also meet people

1554
01:10:26,700 --> 01:10:27,700
who are more in sync with you.

1555
01:10:29,600 --> 01:10:30,733
I hope everyone you meet

1556
01:10:30,733 --> 01:10:32,666
will be someone you click with.

1557
01:10:32,700 --> 01:10:33,933
I hope you can always be yourself.

1558
01:10:35,733 --> 01:10:36,733
[Hope you can be yourself.]

1559
01:10:36,733 --> 01:10:37,600
Okay, thank you.

1560
01:10:38,900 --> 01:10:41,500
So I really hope everyone

1561
01:10:41,500 --> 01:10:44,966
can be true to themselves

1562
01:10:45,000 --> 01:10:46,866
and still be someone's favorite.

1563
01:10:52,533 --> 01:10:53,000
Okay.

1564
01:10:54,133 --> 01:10:54,766
Okay.

1565
01:11:01,666 --> 01:11:02,700
Then let's leave together.

1566
01:11:05,100 --> 01:11:06,233
Let me look at the flowers.

1567
01:11:07,066 --> 01:11:08,766
What's it called? 'Endless Summer'.

1568
01:11:08,800 --> 01:11:11,433
Yeah, it means more summers.

1569
01:11:11,433 --> 01:11:13,333
It looks so pretty.

1570
01:11:14,233 --> 01:11:15,100
Thank you.

1571
01:11:15,100 --> 01:11:16,800
And it's purple, right in my quadrant.

1572
01:11:18,833 --> 01:11:20,333
'Endless Summer'.

1573
01:11:20,333 --> 01:11:21,833
The color chosen was purple.

1574
01:11:21,866 --> 01:11:23,966
My name also has the color in it.

1575
01:11:24,000 --> 01:11:27,000
The meaning is that we can have

1576
01:11:27,000 --> 01:11:28,533
many summers in the future

1577
01:11:28,533 --> 01:11:29,433
and reunite.

1578
01:11:30,100 --> 01:11:32,233
We've already had a perfect ending.

1579
01:11:32,266 --> 01:11:33,400
We're all happy.

1580
01:11:33,433 --> 01:11:34,300
Why does it start raining

1581
01:11:34,300 --> 01:11:35,633
when it's our turn?

1582
01:11:36,666 --> 01:11:37,900
It likes you.

1583
01:11:37,900 --> 01:11:39,166
You come, and the rain comes.

1584
01:11:41,666 --> 01:11:43,733
Let me walk you back.

1585
01:11:43,733 --> 01:11:43,933
Okay.

1586
01:11:43,933 --> 01:11:44,600
It's raining.

1587
01:11:44,633 --> 01:11:45,566
Let's hurry.

1588
01:11:45,600 --> 01:11:46,800
Or you two will get wet.

1589
01:11:46,800 --> 01:11:47,833
It's fine, we're okay.

1590
01:11:47,833 --> 01:11:49,233
Okay, I'm here.

1591
01:11:49,233 --> 01:11:49,633
Bye-bye.

1592
01:11:49,633 --> 01:11:50,866
You guys should head back quickly.

1593
01:11:50,866 --> 01:11:51,500
Sure.

1594
01:11:51,500 --> 01:11:53,166
You three came back together?

1595
01:11:53,200 --> 01:11:53,633
Yeah.

1596
01:11:53,633 --> 01:11:55,566
'Princess' and her two 'guards'.

1597
01:11:55,600 --> 01:11:57,100
Hurry back, it's raining.

1598
01:11:59,233 --> 01:12:00,266
Hurry,

1599
01:12:00,266 --> 01:12:00,966
come in.

1600
01:12:01,000 --> 01:12:02,033
It's raining.

1601
01:12:07,033 --> 01:12:09,100
What about this photo?

1602
01:12:09,900 --> 01:12:12,733
[Peel-apart Films taken
with Pu Yanyan]

1603
01:12:14,833 --> 01:12:15,966
Look at you, is it tough?

1604
01:12:16,000 --> 01:12:18,033
Your feelings are all written
on your face, bro.

1605
01:12:18,033 --> 01:12:19,866
It's tough, really tough.

1606
01:12:20,233 --> 01:12:21,100
I feel like crying.

1607
01:12:21,633 --> 01:12:23,066
Don't cry, bro. Don't be sad.

1608
01:12:24,933 --> 01:12:26,600
Why does this feel like a breakup?

1609
01:12:26,633 --> 01:12:28,300
Why do I feel this way?

1610
01:12:30,666 --> 01:12:31,000
Let's go.

1611
01:12:31,033 --> 01:12:31,633
Are you going?

1612
01:12:31,633 --> 01:12:32,500
Let him be alone for a while.

1613
01:12:44,266 --> 01:12:45,766
Let me take a look.

1614
01:12:45,800 --> 01:12:47,266
It's nice.

1615
01:12:47,266 --> 01:12:48,133
So pretty.

1616
01:12:49,666 --> 01:12:51,900
[Keeping Them]
I'll keep it at my place.

1617
01:12:51,900 --> 01:12:53,233
Okay, as long as you don't throw it away.

1618
01:12:54,533 --> 01:12:55,233
Let me take one.

1619
01:12:57,400 --> 01:12:58,533
I like this one.

1620
01:12:58,533 --> 01:12:59,333
I'll keep this one.

1621
01:13:00,266 --> 01:13:01,366
This one is so cute.

1622
01:13:04,033 --> 01:13:04,700
I'll help you move your luggage later.

1623
01:13:05,000 --> 01:13:06,266
There seems to be an interview, too.

1624
01:13:07,066 --> 01:13:08,500
Alright, pack your bags. Bye-bye.

1625
01:13:15,333 --> 01:13:16,333
I think real love

1626
01:13:16,333 --> 01:13:17,800
means going through some things together.

1627
01:13:17,833 --> 01:13:19,733
It takes time

1628
01:13:19,733 --> 01:13:23,400
to smooth out your rough edges
for each other.

1629
01:13:23,433 --> 01:13:24,666
It needs to happen slowly.

1630
01:13:24,666 --> 01:13:26,566
It's pretty sad.

1631
01:13:26,600 --> 01:13:28,333
Feels pretty tough.

1632
01:13:32,066 --> 01:13:33,766
I think I'm really grateful

1633
01:13:33,800 --> 01:13:36,433
to have met Kelvin Wang on this island.

1634
01:13:36,433 --> 01:13:37,866
Even though the ending

1635
01:13:37,866 --> 01:13:43,266
might not have gone in a sweet direction,

1636
01:13:43,266 --> 01:13:46,066
I feel like this outcome

1637
01:13:46,066 --> 01:13:48,466
is actually quite perfect

1638
01:13:48,466 --> 01:13:50,333
for both of us.

1639
01:13:50,333 --> 01:13:51,233
I don't really

1640
01:13:51,266 --> 01:13:52,800
have any regrets.

1641
01:13:57,833 --> 01:13:59,566
It'll be so interesting
to watch the show later,

1642
01:13:59,600 --> 01:14:00,133
I bet.

1643
01:14:01,833 --> 01:14:03,133
I wanna see how you

1644
01:14:03,133 --> 01:14:04,533
looked for me six, eight times.

1645
01:14:04,533 --> 01:14:06,066
[The Brave Huihui Who Kept Trying]
I really wanna see.

1646
01:14:06,100 --> 01:14:07,100
I wonder if it

1647
01:14:07,100 --> 01:14:08,200
got filmed or not,

1648
01:14:08,233 --> 01:14:08,766
or if it will be kept.

1649
01:14:08,800 --> 01:14:11,333
If this part makes it into your final...

1650
01:14:11,333 --> 01:14:12,633
there must be footage of it.

1651
01:14:14,933 --> 01:14:15,466
At that time,

1652
01:14:15,500 --> 01:14:17,200
you know what one thought I had?

1653
01:14:17,233 --> 01:14:19,266
Anytime in the morning
or in the afternoon,

1654
01:14:19,266 --> 01:14:20,500
I never felt like
the chemistry could happen.

1655
01:14:20,500 --> 01:14:22,100
Only during those personal chats at night,

1656
01:14:22,100 --> 01:14:23,833
that was the way to express your feelings.

1657
01:14:23,866 --> 01:14:25,266
If you want to express your feelings,

1658
01:14:25,266 --> 01:14:26,166
you just go chat with them.

1659
01:14:26,200 --> 01:14:28,666
Talk about how you feel about each other,
that kind of thing.

1660
01:14:28,666 --> 01:14:29,300
The daily activities in the morning,

1661
01:14:29,300 --> 01:14:29,900
I feel like they're just

1662
01:14:29,900 --> 01:14:31,633
a social thing,
like a summer camp for everyone.

1663
01:14:32,466 --> 01:14:33,333
It was like kids

1664
01:14:33,333 --> 01:14:35,133
playing around.

1665
01:14:35,933 --> 01:14:37,933
The destination was always the same.

1666
01:14:37,933 --> 01:14:38,733
It was just Pan (Pan Xiaoyi)

1667
01:14:38,733 --> 01:14:40,233
washing vegetables over there.

1668
01:14:40,266 --> 01:14:41,400
[All the wandering ends
at Pan washing veggies.]

1669
01:14:41,433 --> 01:14:43,733
Doing so frantically.

1670
01:14:48,266 --> 01:14:50,266
Susu (Zhang Xuefei).

1671
01:14:50,266 --> 01:14:52,566
What's up? Missing me again?

1672
01:14:53,533 --> 01:14:55,166
I said, did you miss me again?

1673
01:14:55,200 --> 01:14:56,300
Can't I miss you?

1674
01:14:56,300 --> 01:14:57,966
[Missing You Again]
I just came over to see you.

1675
01:14:58,300 --> 01:14:59,233
Passionfruit flavor.

1676
01:15:00,833 --> 01:15:01,533
[Snack]
Have one.

1677
01:15:03,333 --> 01:15:05,133
You have it. I just had two.

1678
01:15:05,833 --> 01:15:06,466
You have one now,

1679
01:15:06,466 --> 01:15:07,166
and then when we get on the bus later,

1680
01:15:07,200 --> 01:15:07,933
[Considerate]
if you're hungry, have another one.

1681
01:15:08,633 --> 01:15:09,766
So thoughtful.

1682
01:15:09,800 --> 01:15:10,833
Okay.

1683
01:15:11,300 --> 01:15:12,433
Keep one, eat one.

1684
01:15:14,300 --> 01:15:19,933
[The Starer]

1685
01:15:19,933 --> 01:15:21,366
Why are you staring at me like that?

1686
01:15:21,400 --> 01:15:23,400
It makes me not know what to do.

1687
01:15:24,233 --> 01:15:25,633
Draw a heart now.

1688
01:15:26,800 --> 01:15:27,266
Quick.

1689
01:15:30,100 --> 01:15:32,233
Can you draw a heart for us now?

1690
01:15:39,233 --> 01:15:40,333
[Last Announcement]
Attention, all islanders.

1691
01:15:40,333 --> 01:15:41,366
[on the Island of Affection]
Attention, all islanders.

1692
01:15:41,400 --> 01:15:43,633
The confession moment has ended.

1693
01:15:43,633 --> 01:15:45,300
The Island of Affection
will be closing soon.

1694
01:15:48,800 --> 01:15:49,800
It's over, bro.

1695
01:15:52,933 --> 01:15:53,966
We're about to leave this place.

1696
01:15:54,000 --> 01:15:55,100
I really don't want to go.

1697
01:15:56,666 --> 01:15:58,800
In case

1698
01:15:58,833 --> 01:16:00,366
I don't see you...

1699
01:16:00,400 --> 01:16:01,733
Now, your turn.

1700
01:16:02,666 --> 01:16:05,700
Good morning, good afternoon,
and good night.

1701
01:16:09,733 --> 01:16:10,466
So sad.

1702
01:16:12,300 --> 01:16:13,933
Who's going to make me laugh
after I leave you?

1703
01:16:13,933 --> 01:16:14,733
Yeah.

1704
01:16:14,733 --> 01:16:16,566
No one will wake us up tomorrow.

1705
01:16:16,600 --> 01:16:17,800
Who's going to make me laugh?

1706
01:16:18,933 --> 01:16:19,800
I'm actually pretty sad

1707
01:16:19,833 --> 01:16:22,533
because I'm really going to miss everyone.

1708
01:16:22,533 --> 01:16:24,033
It just feels like

1709
01:16:24,500 --> 01:16:25,700
after your student days are over,

1710
01:16:25,700 --> 01:16:27,900
it's really hard to have
this kind of group life again.

1711
01:16:27,900 --> 01:16:29,000
And on the island,

1712
01:16:29,033 --> 01:16:31,266
everyone left behind all their titles,

1713
01:16:31,266 --> 01:16:33,133
social status, and stuff like that.

1714
01:16:33,133 --> 01:16:35,266
So everyone was relatively more genuine.

1715
01:16:35,300 --> 01:16:37,333
I think this kind of life and experience

1716
01:16:37,333 --> 01:16:38,600
are pretty rare.

1717
01:16:39,200 --> 01:16:41,900
Islanders, please head to the beach

1718
01:16:41,900 --> 01:16:44,200
for the official farewell
to the Island of Affection.

1719
01:16:54,200 --> 01:16:56,000
It's time.

1720
01:16:56,000 --> 01:16:57,200
Where's Huihui (Duan Danhui)?

1721
01:16:57,200 --> 01:16:58,466
It's raining.

1722
01:16:58,466 --> 01:16:59,100
Pan (Pan Xiaoyi).

1723
01:16:59,100 --> 01:17:00,133
Okay, thanks.

1724
01:17:00,133 --> 01:17:01,200
Pan (Pan Xiaoyi).

1725
01:17:01,833 --> 01:17:02,866
[Every word gets a reply.]

1726
01:17:02,866 --> 01:17:03,300
Let me take it.

1727
01:17:06,033 --> 01:17:06,933
What are you doing?

1728
01:17:07,900 --> 01:17:09,100
[Realizing It]

1729
01:17:10,333 --> 01:17:12,000
Why did you switch your grip again?

1730
01:17:12,033 --> 01:17:12,833
It's always been like this.

1731
01:17:12,833 --> 01:17:13,500
Like this.

1732
01:17:13,500 --> 01:17:14,733
Weren't you pulling on the left side?

1733
01:17:14,733 --> 01:17:16,600
It's always been like this.

1734
01:17:16,633 --> 01:17:19,733
Holding it this way
feels a bit more secure.

1735
01:17:20,933 --> 01:17:22,966
♪The weather's not cooperating♪

1736
01:17:23,000 --> 01:17:25,033
♪I'll just lie in bed and sleep♪

1737
01:17:25,733 --> 01:17:27,200
If it pours, I'll run back.

1738
01:17:27,233 --> 01:17:29,300
If it pours, we sing a sad song.

1739
01:17:29,300 --> 01:17:30,600
Then we can film

1740
01:17:30,633 --> 01:17:33,033
youthful regret kind of scenes.

1741
01:17:33,033 --> 01:17:34,433
Then we run in the rain.

1742
01:17:35,266 --> 01:17:36,400
They have umbrellas.

1743
01:17:36,433 --> 01:17:37,533
[Stirring Up Jealousy]
Look at them.

1744
01:17:37,533 --> 01:17:38,033
They look so happy.

1745
01:17:38,066 --> 01:17:38,366
♪Hand in hand♪

1746
01:17:38,400 --> 01:17:41,833
♪Step by step, we gaze up high♪

1747
01:17:41,833 --> 01:17:42,700
Didn't they bring an umbrella?

1748
01:17:42,700 --> 01:17:43,300
♪Counting stars♪

1749
01:17:43,300 --> 01:17:46,433
♪One by one, they stitch the sky♪

1750
01:17:46,466 --> 01:17:47,866
What?

1751
01:17:53,266 --> 01:17:55,533
What are you all 'wow'-ing about?

1752
01:17:56,133 --> 01:17:57,166
These two are for you, too.

1753
01:17:57,200 --> 01:17:58,900
The first two drafts of my letter.

1754
01:17:58,900 --> 01:17:59,600
[First Two Drafts
of the Confession Letter]

1755
01:18:00,066 --> 01:18:01,900
They also have different things written.

1756
01:18:01,900 --> 01:18:03,800
This is so awkward,
I kinda don't want to give it to you now.

1757
01:18:03,833 --> 01:18:05,300
Why not?

1758
01:18:05,300 --> 01:18:05,800
It's a bit awkward.

1759
01:18:05,833 --> 01:18:06,666
[Hesitating]
Does it sound fake?

1760
01:18:06,666 --> 01:18:07,733
Not exactly.

1761
01:18:07,733 --> 01:18:09,466
It's just a bit...

1762
01:18:09,500 --> 01:18:10,700
Written just for the sake of writing?

1763
01:18:10,700 --> 01:18:12,400
The same few sentences back and forth.

1764
01:18:16,266 --> 01:18:16,666
Let's go.

1765
01:18:17,266 --> 01:18:18,000
Maybe I shouldn't take it.

1766
01:18:20,833 --> 01:18:21,233
Do you want it?

1767
01:18:23,466 --> 01:18:24,133
Do you want to give it?

1768
01:18:25,900 --> 01:18:27,833
It's a bit awkward.

1769
01:18:27,866 --> 01:18:28,400
Embarrassing.

1770
01:18:31,833 --> 01:18:32,533
[Taking It]
Let's go.

1771
01:18:32,533 --> 01:18:33,666
It really is.

1772
01:18:33,700 --> 01:18:35,500
Put it in your pocket for now.

1773
01:18:35,500 --> 01:18:36,633
Okay.

1774
01:18:37,400 --> 01:18:38,800
[Offering the Umbrella]
You hold the umbrella.

1775
01:18:38,800 --> 01:18:39,600
Why?

1776
01:18:40,033 --> 01:18:41,766
This umbrella's too small, just for you.

1777
01:18:41,800 --> 01:18:42,066
What about you?

1778
01:18:42,066 --> 01:18:42,566
I'll be right behind you.

1779
01:18:44,533 --> 01:18:46,800
[Sneaking a Peek at the Letter]

1780
01:18:47,500 --> 01:18:49,133
[Busted on the Spot]

1781
01:18:49,833 --> 01:18:50,933
Read it later when you get back.

1782
01:18:50,933 --> 01:18:51,866
Okay.

1783
01:18:51,900 --> 01:18:53,533
It's just awkwardly written anyway.

1784
01:18:56,400 --> 01:18:57,033
[Sweet]
You hold it,

1785
01:18:57,033 --> 01:18:58,033
[Sweet]
or your hairstyle will get ruined.

1786
01:19:00,400 --> 01:19:01,200
Hairstyle?

1787
01:19:01,200 --> 01:19:01,533
Yeah.

1788
01:19:01,533 --> 01:19:02,666
It's fine.

1789
01:19:02,700 --> 01:19:03,566
I'll just fix it again.

1790
01:19:05,466 --> 01:19:05,900
Are you cold?

1791
01:19:06,133 --> 01:19:07,766
[Caring]

1792
01:19:07,800 --> 01:19:08,300
No.

1793
01:19:08,666 --> 01:19:09,000
Really?

1794
01:19:09,033 --> 01:19:09,300
Yeah.

1795
01:19:12,866 --> 01:19:14,733
[Two by Two]

1796
01:19:15,300 --> 01:19:16,900
Why is everyone on the island...

1797
01:19:16,900 --> 01:19:18,600
Everyone is going 'wow'.

1798
01:19:18,633 --> 01:19:21,133
Today, the sugar intake
is just a bit too high.

1799
01:19:21,133 --> 01:19:22,366
[Sugar Sick]
I've had it enough, you know?

1800
01:19:22,400 --> 01:19:22,733
Yeah.

1801
01:19:24,533 --> 01:19:25,933
Have you finished?

1802
01:19:25,933 --> 01:19:27,200
Then I'll go.

1803
01:19:27,233 --> 01:19:28,233
What do you want to say?

1804
01:19:28,233 --> 01:19:28,666
Just listen.

1805
01:19:28,666 --> 01:19:30,066
You can hear me loudest

1806
01:19:30,066 --> 01:19:30,733
over here.

1807
01:19:30,733 --> 01:19:31,766
[Expecting]

1808
01:19:31,833 --> 01:19:33,133
[The Island of Affection
The Last Minute Before Closing]

1809
01:19:33,133 --> 01:19:34,633
Words of farewell.

1810
01:19:34,666 --> 01:19:35,466
Now that we're really leaving,

1811
01:19:35,466 --> 01:19:37,500
I really feel a bit reluctant.

1812
01:19:37,500 --> 01:19:40,166
[Staring]
I hope we can be just as genuine

1813
01:19:40,200 --> 01:19:41,700
[Staring]
off the island.

1814
01:19:41,700 --> 01:19:43,033
Just as happy.

1815
01:19:43,066 --> 01:19:46,400
And have fewer worldly troubles.

1816
01:19:46,433 --> 01:19:48,900
Keep more innocence in our hearts.

1817
01:19:49,266 --> 01:19:50,200
[Stay genuine and true. -Zhang Xuefei]
Good.

1818
01:19:50,233 --> 01:19:50,866
Good.

1819
01:19:50,866 --> 01:19:54,966
All the guests, all the staff,

1820
01:19:55,000 --> 01:19:55,633
thank you.

1821
01:19:59,200 --> 01:20:02,066
[Be happy every day. -Ma Haoxiang]
I hope everyone is happy every day.

1822
01:20:02,066 --> 01:20:04,366
I've said what I want to during the day.

1823
01:20:04,400 --> 01:20:05,600
The tears have also been shed.

1824
01:20:05,600 --> 01:20:07,233
Till we meet again, everyone.
Let's keep in touch.

1825
01:20:07,233 --> 01:20:07,733
[Till we meet again, keep in touch.
-Guo Zhentao]

1826
01:20:09,100 --> 01:20:10,400
Coming to this island taught me

1827
01:20:10,433 --> 01:20:13,533
the courage to be brave for love.

1828
01:20:13,533 --> 01:20:15,266
I was really swept up
by everyone's passion.

1829
01:20:15,300 --> 01:20:16,800
[Find the courage to be brave for love.]
So from now on, I'll work hard in life

1830
01:20:16,800 --> 01:20:17,966
[-Sun Shuo]
So from now on, I'll work hard in life

1831
01:20:18,000 --> 01:20:19,000
and be happy every day.

1832
01:20:20,000 --> 01:20:21,500
Thank you, the Island of Affection,

1833
01:20:21,500 --> 01:20:23,033
for taking away a lot of my worries

1834
01:20:23,066 --> 01:20:25,733
and leaving behind so much happiness.

1835
01:20:25,733 --> 01:20:27,733
I hope I always know

1836
01:20:27,733 --> 01:20:29,166
what I truly want.

1837
01:20:29,866 --> 01:20:32,866
If fate allows, we'll meet again.

1838
01:20:32,866 --> 01:20:35,966
I wish everyone smooth sailing
after leaving the island.

1839
01:20:36,000 --> 01:20:37,733
Always be true to yourself.

1840
01:20:38,233 --> 01:20:39,533
No goodbyes.

1841
01:20:40,200 --> 01:20:43,600
Goodbye, Shenzhen.

1842
01:20:43,600 --> 01:20:45,200
Wait for me, Beijing.

1843
01:20:47,466 --> 01:20:49,066
What should I say?

1844
01:20:49,066 --> 01:20:50,366
Let's all keep growing up

1845
01:20:50,400 --> 01:20:51,900
into better adults.

1846
01:20:52,200 --> 01:20:53,533
Goodbye, the Island of Affection.

1847
01:20:53,533 --> 01:20:55,733
See you all again, everyone.

1848
01:20:55,733 --> 01:20:57,566
I'll be happy forever,

1849
01:20:57,600 --> 01:20:58,933
always shining.

1850
01:20:58,933 --> 01:21:00,566
Thank you, everyone.

1851
01:21:00,600 --> 01:21:02,400
Let's get ready to eat.

1852
01:21:03,600 --> 01:21:04,700
Good.

1853
01:21:04,700 --> 01:21:06,166
He is always like this.

1854
01:21:06,666 --> 01:21:07,933
Such a cute little guy.

1855
01:21:08,500 --> 01:21:10,366
How could Beijing possibly wait for you?

1856
01:21:10,400 --> 01:21:11,633
You have to go find it yourself.

1857
01:21:12,833 --> 01:21:14,433
It doesn't wait.

1858
01:21:14,433 --> 01:21:15,733
She'll be there waiting,
and I'll go find her.

1859
01:21:16,066 --> 01:21:17,333
[Wait for Me to Find You]

1860
01:21:17,333 --> 01:21:18,733
Isn't that right?

1861
01:21:18,733 --> 01:21:19,366
Right?

1862
01:21:19,400 --> 01:21:20,066
Yes.

1863
01:21:20,866 --> 01:21:22,400
Yes.

1864
01:21:23,733 --> 01:21:24,633
[Jealous]

1865
01:21:24,666 --> 01:21:25,666
Who said 'wait for me, Beijing'?

1866
01:21:25,666 --> 01:21:26,300
I did.

1867
01:21:26,300 --> 01:21:26,566
I did.

1868
01:21:26,800 --> 01:21:27,833
[Not Too Late to Say It Now]

1869
01:21:29,733 --> 01:21:30,466
You live in Beijing.

1870
01:21:30,500 --> 01:21:31,200
She lives in Beijing, too.

1871
01:21:31,233 --> 01:21:31,533
Yeah.

1872
01:21:31,533 --> 01:21:32,633
How far is it from Xinjiang to Beijing?

1873
01:21:32,933 --> 01:21:34,400
[How far is it from Xinjiang to Beijing?]

1874
01:21:34,833 --> 01:21:36,433
Love knows no distance.

1875
01:21:36,433 --> 01:21:38,233
Love knows no distance.

1876
01:21:41,866 --> 01:21:43,000
I'll never forget

1877
01:21:43,033 --> 01:21:45,533
these 12 days in my life.

1878
01:21:46,800 --> 01:21:48,866
A lot of unexpected things happened.

1879
01:21:48,866 --> 01:21:51,700
These days have been pretty magical.

1880
01:21:51,700 --> 01:21:53,233
I made a lot of great friends.

1881
01:21:53,266 --> 01:21:55,666
Most importantly,
I got to know Ma (Ma Haoxiang).

1882
01:21:55,666 --> 01:21:57,200
And I also got to know myself better.

1883
01:21:57,500 --> 01:21:59,300
For me, this journey of affection

1884
01:21:59,300 --> 01:22:00,500
was unexpected,

1885
01:22:00,500 --> 01:22:02,533
but it was happy.

1886
01:22:02,533 --> 01:22:03,800
Super happy.

1887
01:22:03,833 --> 01:22:05,466
Looking forward
to the journey of affection ahead.

1888
01:22:05,466 --> 01:22:06,900
The journey outside the island.

1889
01:22:06,900 --> 01:22:09,566
I want to say to everyone on the island

1890
01:22:09,600 --> 01:22:11,700
that our meeting was fate.

1891
01:22:11,833 --> 01:22:13,966
Every feast in this world ends.

1892
01:22:14,000 --> 01:22:15,333
I think in the future,

1893
01:22:15,333 --> 01:22:17,233
as long as we still remember each other,

1894
01:22:17,266 --> 01:22:19,366
we will definitely meet again.

1895
01:22:19,833 --> 01:22:21,633
These last few days with everyone

1896
01:22:21,633 --> 01:22:23,366
really made me happy.

1897
01:22:23,400 --> 01:22:24,833
For me, I have no regrets.

1898
01:22:24,833 --> 01:22:26,300
I had a really good time.

1899
01:22:26,300 --> 01:22:28,900
I learned to put myself in others' shoes,

1900
01:22:28,900 --> 01:22:30,800
to think, and to understand others.

1901
01:22:31,433 --> 01:22:33,233
I'm just really grateful

1902
01:22:33,233 --> 01:22:34,166
to have met everyone.

1903
01:22:34,800 --> 01:22:35,800
I hope Qianyu

1904
01:22:35,800 --> 01:22:37,233
and all the friends on the island

1905
01:22:37,233 --> 01:22:38,133
can live better and better

1906
01:22:38,133 --> 01:22:39,566
when we return to our lives.

1907
01:22:39,600 --> 01:22:40,633
Be happy.

1908
01:22:41,700 --> 01:22:42,966
I've grown a lot

1909
01:22:43,000 --> 01:22:44,666
and met a lot of people

1910
01:22:44,666 --> 01:22:46,933
really worth knowing.

1911
01:22:46,933 --> 01:22:49,166
I don't regret it at all.

1912
01:22:49,200 --> 01:22:51,733
And I have no regrets either.

1913
01:22:52,400 --> 01:22:53,800
If I could do it all over again,

1914
01:22:53,800 --> 01:22:54,900
I would definitely come.

1915
01:22:54,900 --> 01:22:56,733
But I wouldn't be the 'catfish' anymore.

1916
01:22:57,833 --> 01:22:59,733
I love 'Love Wins All'.

1917
01:22:59,733 --> 01:23:02,000
I love every islander here.

1918
01:23:03,100 --> 01:23:05,566
The Island of Affection is truly

1919
01:23:05,600 --> 01:23:07,333
a bold, colorful stroke

1920
01:23:07,333 --> 01:23:08,933
in the story of my life.

1921
01:23:10,000 --> 01:23:11,500
This whole journey

1922
01:23:11,500 --> 01:23:13,600
means something extraordinary to me.

